===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|flet||floor of a house; house}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|flet}}, {{m|ang|flett||the ground; the floor of a house; house; dwelling}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*flatją||a flat or level surface, level ground, floor, hallway}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*plad-||flat, broad}}. Cognate with Dutch {{m|nl|vlet||vessel}}, Low German {{m|nds|Flet||an upper bedroom}}, German {{m|de|Fletz}}, {{m|de|Flötz||level ground, threshing floor, hallway, set of rooms or benches}}. More at {{l|en|flat}}.

