==Middle English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang|enm}} {{m|ang|flet|}}, {{m|ang|flett||floor, ground; dwelling, house}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|enm}} {{m|gem-pro|*flatją||floor}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|enm}} {{m|gem-pro|*flataz||flat}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|enm}} {{m|ine-pro|*plat-||flat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/flet/|lang=enm}}

===Noun===
{{enm-noun|pl=flets}}

# the [[floor]], [[ground]]
#: ''Cliued mi saule to þi '''flet'''.'' &mdash; Northern Verse Psalter, 1400
# a [[dwelling]], [[habitation]], [[house]], [[cottage]], [[hall]]
#: ''Þe lorde..Fyndez fire vpon '''flet''', þe [[freke]] þer byside.'' &mdash; Sir Gawain and the Green Knight, 1400
# A (level) piece of ground; a [[battlefield]]
#: ''Wiþ four othre meteþ he ... & fuld hem on þe '''flette'''.'' &mdash; Sir Firumbras, c1380

====Descendants====
* English [[flat]]

