==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|fled}}, {{l|ang|flett}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*flatją||floor}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*flataz||flat}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*plat-||flat}}. Akin to {{cog|ofs|flet|flet, flette|dwelling, house}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/flet/|lang=ang}}

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|n|flet}}

# the [[floor]], [[ground]]
#: ''Heó on '''flet''' gecrong'' &mdash; She sank to the ground.
# a [[dwelling]], [[habitation]], [[house]], [[cottage]], [[hall]]
#: ''Gif ðæt '''flet''' geblódgad wyrþe.'' &mdash; If the house be stained with blood.

