* {{l|ang|fletræst}} f. — couch
* {{l|ang|fletsittend}} m. — sitter in hall, courtier, guest.
* {{l|ang|fletwerod}} n. — hall-troop, body-guard

=====Descendants=====
* Middle English: {{l|enm|flet}}
** English [[flat]]

===Etymology 2===
Likely from {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*flutōną||to float}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*plewd-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*plew-||to float, swim, fly}}; compare {{cog|da|fløde||cream}}, {{cog|is|fleytið||skimming}}, {{cog|no|fløte||cream}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/fleːt/|lang=ang}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|ang|flete}}, {{l|ang|fliet}}, {{l|ang|flyte}}

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|head=flēt|f|flēta}}

# [[cream]], [[skimming]], [[curds]]
#: ''Hwít sealt dó on reám oððe góde '''fléte'''. &mdash; Put white salt into cream or good skimmings.

